Subject: [PATCH] wave: follow native software AP_VLAN creation lifetime

Standard hostapd creates a four-address AP_VLAN before assigning its BSS
MAC through the netdevice ioctl. Allow an initially unattached software
port, implement the DOWN MAC setter, and select its exact active BSS at
first open. Keep that parent pinned across close/reopen and preserve the
existing station, key, multicast and packet lifetime owners.

Reserve headroom before registration and preserve the configured MTU.
Retire never-opened children before wiphy teardown, and reject their
parent-dependent control operations without an assertion. AP_VLAN ports
have no separate MLME; their registration cleanup must not overwrite the
parent management receive filter.

